        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CHR04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>James</forename>
                        <surname>Christie</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1773"/>
                    <death when="1831-02-02"/>
                    <occupation>auctioneer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See also <persName key="CHR02">Thomas Christie</persName>. 
    The one clear reference is on 20 May 1808, 'Christie's, w. MJ (sir Thos More and c.)' , which refers to the auctioneer James 
      Christie (1773-1831), or at least to his premises. An advert in the <title>Morning Chronicle</title> the previous day 
    advertises a sale of pictures assembled in the c17 by William Lenthal (d. 1662), speaker of the Long 
    Parliament, including 'the very celebrated Chef d'ouvre of Holbein, the Chancellor, Sir Thomas Moor and
    his family'. The sale was on Saturday 21st and the pictures 'may be viewed five days preceding the sale,
    and Catalogues had'.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>Morning Chronicle</title>, 19 May 1808</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
